# DAY-STARS on a light scene: Sky_PhysicalShowcase authors a 1 lux sun at EV100 0.53, so its noon sky is ~0.06 cd/m^2
# and the 1.8 cd/m^2 stars blazed at noon before the fix. FIELD_Barn (DAY-STARS.scn) is the brief's scene; this one
# runs while FIELD_Barn's load is over the editor memory cap (6.2 GB > 6144 MB at Open Scene, 10-28).
Дано run Scene "Open Scene Sky_PhysicalShowcase.desce"
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано run Entity "Sun"
Дано --subject selection set SunElevation 40
Дано --subject selection set SunAzimuth 20
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.FOV 70
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,300,0
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0,0.866,-0.5
Тогда-вид 1_day the sun high: blue sky with no stars
Когда run Entity "Sun"
Когда --subject selection set SunElevation -25
Тогда-вид 2_night the sun below the horizon: dark night sky, stars visible
